1
00:01:52,310 --> 00:01:54,182
<v Police> Hello, London Police Department

2
00:01:54,182 --> 00:01:56,548
<v Anna> Yes, I would like to report a robbery

3
00:01:56,548 --> 00:02:01,619
<v Police> Alright, just a minute while I pull up the form. OK, could you give me your first and last name?

4
00:02:01,619 --> 00:02:02,880
<v Anna> Anna Grieg.

5
00:02:02,880 --> 00:02:06,001
<v Police> Anna, Greg? G-R-E-G?

6
00:02:06,001 --> 00:02:09,380
<v Anna> No, Grieg. G-R-I-E-G.

7
00:02:09,380 --> 00:02:13,612
<v Police> Got it. Alright moving on: gender - female. Date of birth?

8
00:02:13,612 --> 00:02:15,894
<v Anna> 15th of March, 1980

9
00:02:15,894 --> 00:02:22,648
<v Police> Alright, thanks. Just a few more personal information questions and then we can address your claim.

10
00:02:22,648 --> 00:02:23,619
<v Anna> Alright

11
00:02:23,619 --> 00:02:25,042
<v Police> What is the address?

12
00:02:25,042 --> 00:02:31,122
<v Anna> 4 Ellendale St. That’s E-L-L-E-N-D-A-L-E

13
00:02:31,122 --> 00:02:38,005
<v Police> Oh right, Ellendale Street. Yeah we’ve had a lot of break-ins in that area lately. And the postal code?

14
00:02:38,005 --> 00:02:40,496
<v Anna> W52AT

15
00:02:40,496 --> 00:02:43,215
<v Police> And are you a citizen of the UK?

16
00:02:43,215 --> 00:02:43,826
<v Anna> No

17
00:02:43,826 --> 00:02:47,211
<v Police> Okay, what type of citizenship do you have?

18
00:02:47,211 --> 00:02:53,809
<v Anna> Well, I lived in the United States for most of my life, but I am actually of Grenadian nationality.

19
00:02:53,809 --> 00:02:58,056
<v Police> Okay, so is that the country that issued your passport?

20
00:02:58,056 --> 00:02:58,715
<v Anna> Yes.

21
00:02:58,715 --> 00:02:59,918
<v Police> Alright.

22
00:03:33,947 --> 00:03:35,599
<v Police> And what is the crime you are reporting?

23
00:03:35,599 --> 00:03:37,376
<v Anna> I already said - a robbery!

24
00:03:37,376 --> 00:03:44,528
<v Police> Oh, right. Sorry, this is about the hundredth robbery report I’ve filled out today. Have you had any prior break-ins?

25
00:03:44,528 --> 00:03:50,183
<v Anna> Um, in the building or just my flat? The unit below mine got broken into last year.

26
00:03:50,183 --> 00:03:52,565
<v Police> No, just your flat.

27
00:03:52,565 --> 00:03:54,285
<v Anna> Oh - then no. Not here.

28
00:03:54,285 --> 00:04:04,573
<v Police> Alright, let’s see here. Can you think of anything that was out of the ordinary around your building, or anyone who may have had reason to do this?

29
00:04:04,573 --> 00:04:12,645
<v Anna> No, it seemed like just a normal evening. I didn’t see anyone suspicious, and can’t think of anyone that would target me specifically.

30
00:04:12,645 --> 00:04:15,296
<v Police> How long has this been your place of residence?

31
00:04:15,296 --> 00:04:24,776
<v Anna> Hm, let me think. I moved in on February 1, and it’s October, so it’s been about 8 months already. Wow, time flies!

32
00:04:24,776 --> 00:04:27,460
<v Police> And that is just Ellendale, yeah?

33
00:04:27,460 --> 00:04:31,191
<v Anna> Yes. I have lived in the UK for just over one year.

34
00:04:31,191 --> 00:04:35,816
<v Police> I see. Can you give me the first and last name of all members of the household?

35
00:04:35,816 --> 00:04:37,364
<v Anna> Actually, I live alone.

36
00:04:37,364 --> 00:04:42,081
<v Police> OK - so no other occupants. And can you give me a brief account of what happened?

37
00:04:42,081 --> 00:04:50,285
<v Anna> I left to go to a dinner party at 6 p.m, and when I returned at 11 I found the place ransacked and a lot of my things gone.

38
00:04:50,285 --> 00:04:52,131
<v Police> Any sign of forced entry?

39
00:04:52,131 --> 00:04:57,563
<v Anna> Yes, the back door was wide open, and it looked like someone used a crowbar to force it open.

40
00:04:57,563 --> 00:05:01,862
<v Police> I see. And just to be clear, was the door locked when you left?

41
00:05:01,862 --> 00:05:02,926
<v Anna> Of course!

42
00:05:02,926 --> 00:05:14,550
<v Police> Hey, you would be surprised how many reports we get where people have failed to lock their doors. Now I need you to list any missing items valued above £200.

43
00:05:14,550 --> 00:05:20,276
<v Anna> So far I’m missing my computer, my purse with my wallet in it, and the TV.

44
00:05:20,276 --> 00:05:24,773
<v Police> OK, Let’s start with the computer. What is the estimated value?

45
00:05:24,773 --> 00:05:26,259
<v Anna> £500.

46
00:05:26,259 --> 00:05:27,751
<v Police> And what is the serial number?

47
00:05:27,751 --> 00:05:31,660
<v Anna> G4168770

48
00:05:31,660 --> 00:05:33,700
<v Police> Thank you, and a visual description?

49
00:05:33,700 --> 00:05:38,947
<v Anna> It is a black 13-inch Pemdas Cloudbook. There is an Oxford sticker on the lid.

50
00:05:38,947 --> 00:05:42,710
<v Police> OK, and could you give a description of the purse?

51
00:05:42,710 --> 00:05:48,235
<v Anna> Sure. It’s a Claude Frieda shoulder bag and the material is silver-colored cloth.

52
00:05:48,235 --> 00:05:49,257
<v Police> Price?

53
00:05:49,257 --> 00:05:50,583
<v Anna> £300.

54
00:05:50,583 --> 00:05:56,304
<v Police> Okay. That concludes my report. I’ll submit it and we’ll let you know of any developments.